      <title>‘The only free thing is a bed’: hospital patients forced to pay as Malawi runs out of medicines</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/nov/25/malawi-healthcare-hospitals-drug-shortage-medicines</link>
      <description>Poor rural families forced to find basic medical supplies as scarcity of foreign exchange paralyses healthcare provision Two days into her stay at Salima district hospital, Maureen Msukwa is still waiting for a painkiller that the hospital pharmacy cannot provide. In the shade of the acacia trees outside the brick maternity block, dozens of relatives sit on woven mats among plastic buckets, cooking pots and basins of laundry. Inside, Msukwa, 25, a pregnant mother from Kasache village in…</description>
