      <title>Why pharma firms are going to Earth’s orbit in search of new cancer drugs</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/nov/04/us-firm-varda-space-industries-manufacturing-drugs-in-space</link>
      <description>A space capsule 300 miles above us is growing the tiny crystals of a potential cancer drug in microgravity Roughly 300 miles above our heads, three washing machine-sized capsules are orbiting the Earth. Inside one of them, tiny crystals of a potential cancer drug are being grown in the weightlessness of space. The others are testing heat protection materials and navigation systems for when the capsules plunge back through Earth’s atmosphere at hypersonic speeds. Together, they represent a…</description>
