      <title>Boom in weight-loss drugs could lead to fall in beer sales, Heineken warns UK pubs</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/23/weight-loss-drugs-beer-sales-heineken-british-pubs-wegovy</link>
      <description>World’s second largest brewer says use of drugs such as Wegovy can reduce desire to drink alcohol Heineken has warned British bars and pubs that the boom in popularity of weight-loss drugs could lead to a fall in sales of beer and cider. The world’s second-largest brewer sent a presentation to British hospitality customers earlier this month that said the use of GLP-1 medication – such as Ozempic and Wegovy – could reduce the desire to drink alcohol . This in turn could result in “fullness and…</description>
